<h1>Snake Game</h1>

<p>Click on the Snake Client nav link to start!</p>

<nav>How to use:</nav>
<li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Enter your desirable user name in the 'User ID' box(You cannot change User ID after connected to the server).</li>
<li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Change Server Address and Port number if needed.</li>
<li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Click 'Connect' button to begin play.</li>
<li><strong>Step 4:</strong> Move your snake with keyboard arrow keys or WASD.</li>
<li><strong>Step 5:</strong> Enjoy the game!</li>
<div>&nbsp</div>
<li><strong></strong> Recommended to play in full screen.</li>
<div>&nbsp</div>
<nav>Snake Game implementation specification:</nav>
<li><strong>1:</strong> Using async and await to handle stable network connection and prevent override.</li>
<li><strong>2:</strong> Use of logging for almost all functions we wrote to keep track of any unexpected errors.</li>
<li><strong>3:</strong> Alert message shows up on canvas(it updates frequently).</li>
<li><strong>4:</strong> Client sends the keyinput message only once on a frame.</li>
<li><strong>5:</strong> User can use both WASD and arrow keys to control the snake. It makes user to use whatever button layout they are comfortatble with.</li>
<li><strong>6:</strong> Use of futuristic game images for both background and wall to make the game look more like production version.</li>
<li><strong>7:</strong> Added pulse effect for the power up object to make game more dynamic.</li>
<li><strong>8:</strong> Alert message shows up on canvas(it updates frequently)</li>
<li><strong>9:</strong> Changed layout of HUD so user can easily tack of game stats.</li>
<li><strong>10:</strong> Added ranking system based on each snake's live score.</li>

